"There's no way out.",
"It isn't easy being a god.take yesterday for example.first there was Zeus's temple-warming party:all those relatives you hadn't seen for millennia;all those offspring you didn't know you had.of course,brother Zeus was there with his wife Hera - the perfect hosts as ever.kronos too.dear old dad,I suppose it was nice to see him again after all this time.ha,I remember when he first took me to the seaside.^ \"Poseidon,\" he'd called as I paddled in the shallows. \"Poseidon,don't you wander out too far now.stay close to the shore;you know you can't swim.\"^ How that used to embarrass me!there I am,God of the Sea no less and I couldn't even swim - still can't come to think of it.have you any idea how difficult it is to look god-like and awe-inspiring clad in a pair of red water-wings?^ Never mind,that's the least of my worries right now.you see,the party turned out to be little more than a pretext designed to lure us deities,en masse,to a meeting.and it worked.there we were,eating and drinking and making merry;everything was just fine.then,part-way through - I think we were a year or so into the party which would make it thirty AD or thereabouts - Zeus cleared his throat.^ \"Er,could I have your attention please?\" he said,tapping a wine glass with his fruit knife. \"Excuse me.er,you at the back.persephone.be so good as to pipe down for a moment would you?thank you so much dear.^ \"Gentlemen,\" he began, \"our religious monopoly is being eroded!wherever you look new gods are coming to the fore.yes,I know,we've seen them come and we've seen them go.but some are here to stay;just look at how we underestimated the Romans!now I foresee a new threat.something which threatens irrevocable damage.something so potentially pervasive that it may eventually usurp us.christianity,gentlemen,is our enemy;and I for one do not intend to go down without a fight!\"^ This was rousing stuff!everyone who could stand was on their feet,clapping and cheering.^ \"I propose,\" continued Zeus, \"that we tighten our slack attitudes,rout our complacent outlooks and rid ourselves of these pot-bellies.only then will we be fit to take on this challenge with the necessary courage and vitality.\"^ The cheers were not so loud now.but Zeus had us on the run.he launched into his closing speech. \"To this end I intend to set each and every one of you a task to test your mettle.\" He glanced about the room. \"Now,who shall be first?ah...yes...poseidon.\"^ And that was it.there wasn't even time to get a sick note.zeus handed me a slip of paper,there was this flash and a clap of thunder.and here I am,at the gateway to The Underworld. ~Myth.version 1.0.copyright (c) 1989 Magnetic Scrolls Ltd.~",
