"^the helmet begins to pulsate in your grasp,as if your touch had awakened it from some deep slumber.a soft blue light bathes the room,its growing intensity pacing the ever-quickening throb of the helmet as,together,they build toward a crescendo of light and sound.just as this sensory duet reaches its apocalyptic climax,the room about you seems to drain away like molten wax.as suddenly as it began,the barrage assaulting your senses is gone and wispy shapes begin to form around you.the shapes take on substance and you find yourself back in the temple of Zeus atop mount Olypus.^well,it looks as though things really livened up after you left.drained flagons and drunken deities,spilled wine and ale,discarded robes.oh yes,this was some party.^one of the semi-conscious bodies littering the floor raises its head and stares at you.the bloodshot eyes and pallid complexion make Zeus almost unrecognizable.he beckons you toward him and takes the helmet from you.^ \"Well done Poseidon,\" he says. \"It seems I misjudged you.you are indeed worthy of a place here on Olympus.\" He glances around the room. \"Hades,\" he calls, \"I believe this belongs to you.\" He rolls the helmet across the floor and under a nearby table where it seems to strike something solid.a stifled moan issues from beneath the table-cloth.the cloth lifts and the face of Hades peers out from beneath it.he grunts non-committally before sliding back into unconsciousness.^ \"Well,drinks all round I think,\" says Zeus brightening noticeably.he hands you a goblet of wine.^ \"Cheers!and welcome home.\"~Congratulations,you have won.",
