"We play a variation on the game of Blackjack.basically the object of the game is to obtain a hand whose total is as close to,but does not exceed,twenty-one.all cards count as their face value apart from the ace which may be regarded as one or eleven.an ace and a picture card constitute 'blackjack' and this is the best possible hand.at the beginning of a hand each player is dealt a card and places a bet based on the strength of that card.once all the bets have been made a second card is dealt until each player holds two cards.each player in turn may then ask for additional cards by telling the dealer to 'twist';these cards are dealt face-up for all to see,unlike the first two.when the player is satisfied with his hand he tells the dealer that he wishes to 'stick' and the dealer turns to the next player until everybody is satisfied.at this point all hands are declared and the one closest to twenty-one wins,unless a blackjack is declared.should a player's hand total less than twelve after his first two cards are dealt he is obliged to inform the dealer who will deal additional cards until the hand totals at least twelve.the winner of a hand receives all monies bet on that round.additionally he receives the amount which he himself bet.^ \"We have a house limit of fifty obols and a minimum stake of five.i win all drawn hands and any party may depart the game at his own discretion.i hope this is clear.",
